      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "We're still inside `except ... as e` here, so the traceback keeps the failed forward's tensors alive. I think this only cleans up the *previous* failure. Could we set a flag and run `gc.collect()` + `empty_cache()` after the try/except instead?",
